# Claude Code worktrees: local scratch checkouts, never part of the project
.claude/worktrees/

# Listening history, in every shape it leaves the app in.
#
# None of these belongs in the repository under any circumstances. A backup is
# six years of what the user listened to; a sync batch is the same thing in a
# text format, which makes it *easier* to paste or commit by accident than a
# binary .db is; a CSV export is the same again in the most portable form of
# all. They live in ~/evergreen-backups/ or similar, outside the repo.
#
# Matched by extension anywhere in the tree rather than by directory, because
# the risk is a file saved into the repo root by mistake — a picker defaulting
# somewhere, an adb pull run from the wrong working directory.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
evergreen-backup-*
evergreen-batch-*
*.evergreen.jsonl
evergreen-*.csv

# IDE state that records the serial number of whichever device was selected
/.idea/deploymentTargetSelector.xml
